# autonomy/log.jsonl is append-only: every nightly job (sentinel, darkocean,
# memoryhole, anchor, this discovery pass) appends exactly one line and never
# edits an existing one. Two jobs appending within the same window both diff
# as "insert after the last line", which git's default line-based merge sees
# as the same location and refuses to reconcile on its own — proven for real
# on 2026-08-16 (see tools/commit-and-push.sh for the incident and the rest of
# the fix). The built-in `union` driver keeps both sides' lines instead of
# conflicting, which is exactly correct for a file no line is ever removed
# from or changed in.
autonomy/log.jsonl merge=union
